// Walking into Karkand's sloped statics, checking that the soldier never hangs in the air
// (`NoHang`: off the ground without moving for over 0.3 s fails). The jersey barrier by the
// square (`concretebarrier`) has a beam (`beam_01`) leaning on it at 57.5 degrees, a little
// steeper than soldiers walk up, and sandbags a hand's width beside it: dropped into the
// crevice between the barrier's top and the beam a soldier used to hang there, never grounded
// (see `walks_into_sloped_statics_without_wedging` in game_shared's soldier_movement tests);
// now he stands in it and walks or jumps out. Then walking and sprint-jumping at the barrier
// from all round and off the tops of the barrier and the sandbags, and walking into tilted
// rocks, a fallen lamp post and a wreck's wheel. Gulf of Oman: move_sloped_oman.ron.
// client --scenario scenarios/movement/move_sloped_statics.ron --out target/scenarios/move/sloped_statics
